=== Tracking polls ===
During the last two weeks of the campaign, magazine [[Mladina]], in association with Ninamedia agency, was running a [[tracking poll]] to monitor the trends of changes in support for all three candidates. The poll included n=100 daily with n=200 on the last day of the poll. The final prediction of the poll on Friday, 9 November, indicated 43.8% for Türk, 33.6% for Pahor, and 22.6% for Zver, what would result in a second round being necessary. Support for Zver was more or less stable during the two weeks, slightly above 20%. Long-term trend indicated a slight fall of support for Türk<ref>{{cite news|title=Kdo bo zmagal?|url=http://www.mladina.si/117590/kdo-bo-zmagal/|accessdate=9 November 2012|newspaper=Mladina|date=9 November 2012}}</ref> with the support beginning to rise again in the last days before the election. While the poll first allowed the possibility of Türk being elected in the first round already, the final prediction stated that Türk and Pahor will face the second round.<ref>{{cite web|author= |url=http://www.mladina.si/117654/zadnja-napoved-t-rku-43-8-odstotka-drugi-krog-bo-tesen/ |title=Zadnja napoved: Türku 43,8 odstotka. Drugi krog bo tesen. |publisher=Mladina.Si |accessdate=2012-12-04}}</ref>

Journal [[Delo (newspaper)|Delo]] ran a tracking poll during the last week of the campaign. Similarly, the final prediction indicated 44% for Türk, 33% for Pahor and 23% for Zver. In the last two days, the poll indicated that some of supporters of Türk migrated to Pahor.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.delo.si/novice/volitve/3-delova-meritev-javnega-mnenja-turk-44-pahor-33-zver-23.html |title=3. Delova meritev javnega mnenja: Türk 44%, Pahor 33%, Zver 23% |publisher=Delo.si |accessdate=2012-12-04}}</ref>

